      "body": "The Ralph comment reminds me of an old conversation: \r\nhttps://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/33464#pullrequestreview-3813897610\r\n\r\n>> As a follow-up, I think we can give every outbound onion connection a separate network_id, because they all look distinct to external observers.\r\n\r\n>Just to add this info also here for others reading this: this is not helpful because both current functions of network_id, inv scheduling and getaddr caching, do not apply to outbounds anyway (https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/34456). If we use network_id for additional things in the future, we could revisit.\r\n\r\nSo maybe we should revisit it with this PR, which also affects outbounds?",
